# GitHub repo setup

Reference: `ops-github/data/github-policy.json`

## New project (no origin remote)

1. Ask repo name → validate with `check-repo-name.js`
2. If name exists on GitHub → **stop** and ask user for another name
3. Ask owner: individual account or organization (`list-owners.js`)
4. Description: user input OR auto-generated from project
5. Create **private** repo via `create-repo.js`
6. If owner is an org → grant default teams from policy (`ACME OPS - READ-ONLY` read, `ACME OPS - VIBECODERS` write)

## Existing project (origin configured)

Do not create a new repo. Push only via `push-to-github` skill.
